From 5f85f2e48174620090860d395c1c6c62ba81dcf7
Subject: bevy_image: trigger reduce_image_sizes on dimensions, not bytes
Origin: https://github.com/robtfm/bevy/commit/5f85f2e48174620090860d395c1c6c62ba81dcf7
Date: 2026-05-21T13:21:22+01:00

Switch the `reduce_image_sizes` resize trigger from total-byte threshold
to per-dimension threshold. Catches long-and-thin oversized textures
that the byte check missed when they sat under 4MB total but exceeded
wgpu's per-device dim cap (causing `create_texture` validation panics
mid-bake — observed at 17855x100 RGBA8).

Parameterise the resize target as a single per-platform constant:
wasm keeps the aggressive 1024-pixel cap (memory-bounded); native uses
8192, which is just below wgpu's typical 16384 hard cap on every
desktop GPU. Downstream BC7 reprocessing replaces textures with <=1024
anyway, so native fidelity at this stage doesn't matter — the resize
is purely to dodge the validation panic on initial load.
